file: macros/src/subject.rs
breaks: A struct forwards a trait to the field that names it, whichever home implements it, a partial block included, and not to the bare field beside it, as `docs/decisions/a-fields-trait-may-be-a-partial-blocks.md` and `docs/structs.md` say.
expect: killed
witness: s0=struct-trait s1=none path=block

find:
            (_, Some(named), _) => Ok(*named),
replace:
            (_, Some(_), Some(bare)) => Ok(*bare),
            (_, Some(named), _) => Ok(*named),
